  "adaptations_and_remaining_gaps": [
    "CellFilterCell is an owning Rust adapter with external allocator metadata, not a repr(C) native Cell ABI. Native mutable Cell.index/Objects fields and unrestricted raw extension access are not publicly exposed; safe target iteration and explicit prepend are controlled adapters.",
    "Current LocalArray<i32,10> remains48 bytes versus native56; CellRecord56 versus64 and MapNode<CellRecord>64 versus72 remain open layout/allocation-byte gaps. No LocalArray representation or fake padding was changed.",
    "Native virtual Free override counts are retained in the fixture but not matched to invented Rust counters. The i32 incremental stride/retention observation is scoped; arbitrary allocator subclass overrides, generic alignment and allocator byte behavior are not proved.",
    "Rust discarded nodes release reset-protection leases despite skipped Target Drop. Native has no such lease system. Non-incremental BaseAllocator arguments reclaim node storage as a Rust extension; native CellFilter object nodes use IncAllocator. Retained pointers to discarded nodes are outside the safe adapter contract.",
    "Rust panic recovery drains remaining targets and releases storage before resuming the first destructor panic. Native throwing noexcept destructors are not claimed equivalent. Copy-failure recovery preserves the previous reachable chain and releases the unpublished node lease.",
    "Borrowed observer payloads keep discard tests free of intentionally leaked external allocations; Miri leak checking stays enabled. Payload covariance and conditional Send/Sync/Unpin are checked for the owning adapter. No new public reentrant whole-owner observer or iterator auto-trait equivalence is claimed.",
    "Point/index observations and nine compiler declaration joins establish this bounded callable slice, not universal payload ABI/address-sensitive move equivalence or global API/test completeness. The global ledger remains unchanged."
